From: webos-wpe-browser <poudelswastik@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Allow the private runtime to use its packaged CA bundle

The installed app cannot traverse a shared /tmp CA directory left mode 0700
by a root diagnostic run. Read WPE_BROWSER_CA_FILE through secure_getenv so
normal app processes can use their immutable packaged bundle directly.
Certificate and hostname verification are unchanged. Privileged execution
ignores the environment override, retaining the configured system store.

Upstream: not submitted (application-specific private runtime).
---
--- a/lib/system/certs.c
+++ b/lib/system/certs.c
@@ -125,8 +125,13 @@
 #endif
 
 #ifdef DEFAULT_TRUST_STORE_FILE
+	/* The app's immutable CA bundle has a runtime installation path. Do not
+	 * depend on a shared /tmp file owned by a previous execution user. */
+	const char *trust_file = secure_getenv("WPE_BROWSER_CA_FILE");
+	if (trust_file == NULL || trust_file[0] == '\0')
+		trust_file = DEFAULT_TRUST_STORE_FILE;
 	ret = gnutls_x509_trust_list_add_trust_file(
-		list, DEFAULT_TRUST_STORE_FILE, crl_file, GNUTLS_X509_FMT_PEM,
+		list, trust_file, crl_file, GNUTLS_X509_FMT_PEM,
 		tl_flags, tl_vflags);
 	if (ret > 0)
 		r += ret;
